      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Perineal endometrioma has been reported in reproductive-aged women following perineal trauma. The common presentation is a perineal mass with cyclic pain coincident with the menstrual cycle in a woman with a history of perineal laceration. Curative treatment is possible with complete surgical excision. No reports of perineal endometrioma occurring during pregnancy have been published before."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE",
          "content": "A case of perineal endometrioma occurred during pregnancy. The patient had a perineal mass that enlarged, with worsening pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "A perineal endometrioma may progress during pregnancy. Proper diagnosis is important, and treatment with surgical excision should be considered before attempting subsequent pregnancies."
        }
      ]},
